From: Holodor <holodor@bonesaw.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: q6afe: retry DEVICE_START after a timeout and accept EALREADY

On the Retroid Pocket 5 (SM8250) the DisplayPort AFE port (0x6020, HDMI
over DP) often fails its first DEVICE_START after boot or after the PCM has
been idle: the DSP does not answer within TIMEOUT_MS, the prepare fails,
and the stream the user started is silent. The next start works. If the
failed start is repeated the DSP answers EALREADY (status 9) from then on,
so the port had in fact been started by the command that "timed out"; the
acknowledgement was late or lost.

Treat it that way: when DEVICE_START times out, send it once more, and take
an EALREADY answer as success. The port's DEVICE_STOP on close resets the
DSP side either way.
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c	2026-10-07 22:27:30.028695742 +0900
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c	2026-10-07 22:27:30.037319736 +0900
@@ -369,6 +369,7 @@
 #define AFE_API_VERSION_CODEC_DMA_CONFIG	1
 
 #define TIMEOUT_MS 3000
+#define ADSP_EALREADY 0x9
 #define AFE_CMD_RESP_AVAIL	0
 #define AFE_CMD_RESP_NONE	1
 #define AFE_CLK_TOKEN		1024
@@ -1713,6 +1714,22 @@
 	start->port_id = port_id;
 
 	ret = afe_apr_send_pkt(afe, pkt, port, AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START);
+	if (ret == -ETIMEDOUT) {
+		/*
+		 * The DSP sometimes starts the port but answers late or not at
+		 * all (seen on the HDMI-over-DP port, first start after idle).
+		 * Ask once more; an "already started" answer means the first
+		 * command did go through.
+		 */
+		dev_warn(afe->dev, "AFE start for port 0x%x timed out, retrying\n",
+			 port_id);
+		ret = afe_apr_send_pkt(afe, pkt, port, AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START);
+		if (ret == -EINVAL && port->result.status == ADSP_EALREADY) {
+			dev_info(afe->dev, "AFE port 0x%x was already started\n",
+				 port_id);
+			ret = 0;
+		}
+	}
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(afe->dev, "AFE enable for port 0x%x failed %d\n",
 			port_id, ret);
